Rex::Rancher::Server/Agent write no `node-ip` (and no `node-external-ip`) into config.yaml (_build_agent_config knows server, token, node-name, node-label). On multi-homed hosts RKE2/K3s take the address of the default route.

Seen 2026-10-31 on synapse (kubernetes-ocp k248 live test): eno1 192.168.0.165 (default route, other LAN) + vlan30 10.230.30.50 (cluster network). The node registered with InternalIP 192.168.0.165, which the CP otho cannot reach. Result: Cilium VXLAN broken in one direction, nfd-worker could not deliver, pulls via the NodePort mirror hung. Fixed by hand with `node-ip: 10.230.30.50` + agent restart; InternalIP was right afterwards and NFD labelled at once.

Wanted: options `node_ip` and `node_external_ip` (string or list, for dual-stack) on install_server and install_agent, written as `node-ip` / `node-external-ip`. Same on rke2 and k3s. A re-run must not change a running node's node-ip unasked (same reasoning as node-name, Node.pm:149), or at least must say so.

Done means: tests for the config construction in both modes, POD. OCP follows on its own card and passes the join address.

